### Passkeys (WebAuthn)
### Routes: /api/passkeys/*
###
### Passkey registration/authentication is a challenge/response handshake that needs
### a real browser authenticator (Face ID, Touch ID, Windows Hello, a security key),
### so the register/finish and authenticate/finish steps CANNOT be completed from a
### .http file — the `response` payload is produced by the browser's WebAuthn API.
###
### These requests are included for completeness and to exercise the begin/status/
### management endpoints. The begin endpoints are public; list/delete require auth.

@credentialId = REPLACE_WITH_CREDENTIAL_ID

### Begin registration — returns WebAuthn creation options + a sessionId (public)
# @name registerBegin
POST {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/register/begin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "My Laptop"
}
# => 200 { "options": {...}, "sessionId": "..." }

### Finish registration (public) — `response` must come from navigator.credentials.create()
POST {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/register/finish
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "My Laptop",
  "sessionId": "{{registerBegin.response.body.sessionId}}",
  "response": { "REPLACE_WITH": "browser WebAuthn attestation response" }
}

### Begin authentication — returns assertion options + a sessionId (public, no body)
# @name authBegin
POST {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/authenticate/begin
# => 200 { "options": {...}, "sessionId": "..." }

### Finish authentication (public) — `response` must come from navigator.credentials.get()
# @name authFinish
POST {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/authenticate/finish
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sessionId": "{{authBegin.response.body.sessionId}}",
  "response": { "REPLACE_WITH": "browser WebAuthn assertion response" }
}

### Passkey/secret-store status (public)
GET {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/status
# => 200 { "hasPasskeys": ..., "isUnlocked": ..., "requiresPassword": ... }

### Unlock the encrypted secret store with a fresh passkey assertion
### Needs the single-use authTicket (60s) from authenticate/finish above; a bare
### credential ID is rejected. With auth on, the passkey must be your own (403).
POST {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/unlock
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "authTicket": "{{authFinish.response.body.authTicket}}"
}
# => 200 { "message": "Secret store unlocked successfully" }
# => 400 without authTicket, 401 unknown/used/expired ticket

### List the current user's passkeys (requires auth)
GET {{apiUrl}}/passkeys
# => 200 { "passkeys": [ { "id": ..., "name": ..., "createdAt": ... } ] }

### Delete one of your passkeys (requires auth; you can only delete your own)
DELETE {{apiUrl}}/passkeys/{{credentialId}}
# => 200 { "message": "Passkey deleted successfully" }
